-- title:
--   Stalks of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp) are valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion `coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`, the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series $j$-numerator. Write $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of schemes of the maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the subalgebras `chartAlg A ↥K {j}` and `chartAlg A ↥K {j⁻¹}` into the middle algebra, and `toBase` the induced morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z \in X$, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase`, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ and that this stalk has Krull dimension at most $1$. Then there exist a valuation subring $V$ of $K$ and a ring isomorphism $e : \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \simeq V$ such that: every element of $A$ maps into $V$; every element of the maximal ideal of $A$ maps into the nonunits of $V$; for every $P \in A[T]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$; $e(\varpi_z)$ is the image of $\varpi$ in $K$; and for every $a \in A$, $e$ sends the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $a$ to the image of $a$ in $K$.
--
--   This is the passage from points to valuations for the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the local ring at $p$: a point of the special fibre whose local ring has dimension at most one gives a valuation subring of the function field $K$ dominating $A$, normalised so that $j$ is a unit-like parameter in the sense of the third clause. The three clauses on $V$ together with the compatibility of $e$ with $A$ are exactly what the later identification of the two branches above $p$ requires, and the statement is used in the construction of the valuation subrings attached to the first and second components of the curve model of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_valuationSubring_ringEquiv_stalk_of_ringKrullDim_le_one_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

